From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000013 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Philippov <paul@thingino.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 10:15:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mips: xburst: t30: keep sensor MCLK pinmux with V4L2

The T30 platform omitted MCLK_PORTA whenever CONFIG_VIDEO_V4L2 was enabled.
That leaves the clock framework running cgu_cim at the requested rate but
does not route the clock to the physical sensor pin. Sensors consequently
NACK their I2C address after a V4L2-enabled kernel boots.

The out-of-tree TX-ISP capture driver needs the same SoC pinmux as the
non-V4L2 driver. Keep the base MCLK_PORTA entry independent of the generic
V4L2 core configuration. CONFIG_SOC_MCLK remains available to the in-tree
TX-ISP configuration as before.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@thingino.com>
---
 arch/mips/xburst/soc-t30/common/platform.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/xburst/soc-t30/common/platform.c b/arch/mips/xburst/soc-t30/common/platform.c
index a4ad8b9..fe9dc31 100644
--- a/arch/mips/xburst/soc-t30/common/platform.c
+++ b/arch/mips/xburst/soc-t30/common/platform.c
@@ -49,9 +49,7 @@ struct jz_gpio_func_def platform_devio_array[] = {
 #ifdef CONFIG_I2C2_PC27_PC28
 		I2C2_PORTC,
 #endif
-#ifndef CONFIG_VIDEO_V4L2
 	MCLK_PORTA,
-#endif
 #ifdef CONFIG_SOC_MCLK
 	MCLK_PORTA,
 #endif
-- 
2.51.0
